WEBVTT

00:00:01.748 --> 00:00:08.829
Job Agent: help from Claude
Optional. Without it you still get templates.

00:00:08.829 --> 00:00:10.702
Way 1: no key needed
On an accepted job, press "Copy for Claude"

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:14.186
It copies one message
The job, your profile, how the documents are written, and the rule: never invent anything

00:00:14.186 --> 00:00:20.392
Paste it into a Claude chat
Claude writes the CV and letter from your own material, then you copy the answer

00:00:20.392 --> 00:00:22.781
Paste the answer back
Into the box under the job

00:00:22.781 --> 00:00:26.593
Make the documents
The app checks the answer and writes the CV and letter in your layout

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:32.612
A short report comes with it
What was emphasized, and what was not claimed because your CV does not show it

00:00:32.612 --> 00:00:37.835
Read it, correct it, send it yourself
A tailored draft built only from your own CV and profile

00:00:37.835 --> 00:00:44.473
The same for your CV
My CV and profile: "Copy for Claude" reads an uploaded CV into your profile

00:00:44.473 --> 00:00:52.905
Way 2: your own Anthropic API key
Settings > AI and services. Use is billed to your key.

00:00:52.905 --> 00:01:00.985
Then one click: "Write with AI"
The draft is written through Anthropic's API and lands under the job

00:01:00.985 --> 00:01:11.826
Each request to Anthropic is listed
Settings > Network activity names the material it carried
